WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.001
[music playing]

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.369
 Cameron, Mike,
congratulations.

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.071
It is now down to the two
of you to decide who's

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:06.673
going to go home with the
title of "Forged in Fire"

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.475
champion and a
check for $10,000.

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:11.244
Now, this final
round of competition,

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.979
we're going to be sending you
guys back to your home forges

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.781
to build not one but two
iconic multi tools and weapons

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:17.016
from Russia.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:22.689
And that weapon is
the Spetsnaz shovel.

00:00:25.224 --> 00:00:28.227
Originating in the 19th century,
these all-purpose shovels

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:30.829
were adapted for use by
the Russian special forces,

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:31.964
the Spetsnaz.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.533
These versatile
shovels were used

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:37.236
as entrenching tools, oars for
rafting, and even as cookware.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.205
The Soviet military
units eventually

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.808
trained to use the Spetsnaz
shovel as a weapon.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.543
The short handle is
made for quick moves

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.077
in close quarter combats.

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:47.380
These shovels featured
deadly sharp edges

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.515
that can be used for
anything from chopping wood,

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:52.352
to slashing flesh, or
even thrown at a target.

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.220
This utilitarian
tool can be seen

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.689
wielded in season 3
of History Channel's

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:58.825
hit survival series "Alone."

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:02.128
You guys will have four days to
work on your Spetsnaz shovels.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.228
So good luck.

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.097
We'll see you in four days.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:07.967
 Good luck.

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:09.302
My name is Cameron Lafrance.

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:12.105 line:8%
I am 20 years old from
Warner Robins, Georgia.

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:14.841
I got into metal works
thanks to my father.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:18.611
It's really what sparked, no pun
intended, my drive for working

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.146
with metal and fire.

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:23.115
I have a lot of steel to
move and a very thin blade

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:26.786
to forge out, so
hopefully all goes well.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:29.155
I start off with these two
pieces of leaf spring, just

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:32.859
to see if I can get it
forged down to parameters.

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:36.195
And then I noticed a piece of
W1 that I had laying around.

00:01:36.261 --> 00:01:40.200
It's 2 inch round stock,
so I know for a fact

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.169
that it's enough material for
the job I'm needing it to do.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.703
I'm going to keep
stretching it out

00:01:44.803 --> 00:01:47.373
and then working on the width.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.009
I got to still flatten
out one of my billets.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.277
Woo, that's hot.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.312
I'm getting the handle
and blade junction

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.481
merged up and then quenched.

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:58.517
I have to make sure that
they're both exactly the same

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:00.520
but still very confident
that I can do it.

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:04.423
That looks pretty badass,
if I don't say so myself.

00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:05.825
I feel like I've
gotten to a place now

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:08.527
to wear my blades are
ready for the heat treat.

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:09.395
Here we go.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.569
The sound I want to hear.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:17.737
End of day three.

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:20.406
I am very happy to finally
have all these shovel

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.175
heads forged out, hardened.

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:24.276
Can't wait for a fourth
day to get these fit

00:02:24.376 --> 00:02:26.746
and finished up and out of here.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:29.916
I've had a lot of good luck in
my past with one special girl,

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:32.485
so I go ahead and
put my girlfriend's

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:34.787
name in Russian on
the handle, just

00:02:34.853 --> 00:02:36.489
as a hopeful good luck charm.

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.892
And if it doesn't work,
then I know who to blame.

00:02:42.194 --> 00:02:43.062
 My name is Mike Powell.

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:44.664
I'm from Hastings, Florida.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.366 line:8%
I make blades as often as I
can, usually a couple of hours

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.702 line:8%
in the morning before
work and then as much time

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.270
as my wife will let
me on the weekend.

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:54.206
She sacrifices a lot of
our one-on-one time for me

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:56.075
to be in my shop making blades.

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:59.378
If I win the 10,000, I'm going
to get my wife something nice

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.247
that we can enjoy together.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.015
I'm going to forge
out these shovels

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.218
and see if I can win this.

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:07.020
I got it about
drawn out to length.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:09.388
I haven't quite got
it as wide as I want.

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.457
I'm not sure I have
enough material.

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:14.026
I'll go cut me another piece
of steel for the second one,

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:16.629
drop it in the forge.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:17.863
That ought to do it.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.098
About three blows in--

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:20.433
Whoa!

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.069
--the whole end of the
billet just explodes.

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:24.603
Wow.

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:26.505
What the heck?

00:03:26.605 --> 00:03:28.808
Never seen a piece
of steel do that.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.242
Now I've got one piece left.

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.345
This sucks.

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:34.780
No way.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.015
This is my third attempt.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:36.849
Do over.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.117
I take my time.

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:39.518
I keep my steel to
the right temperature.

00:03:39.585 --> 00:03:43.122
It didn't explode on me
this time, so it worked out.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:44.991
I never built anything
like this before.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.926
I never even thought about
building anything like this

00:03:47.993 --> 00:03:48.928
before.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:51.965
But honestly, I loved it.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:52.998
It was a challenge.

00:03:53.098 --> 00:03:54.333
It was a learning experience.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.902
It made me a better smith.

00:03:55.969 --> 00:03:57.203
So I learned.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:59.305
I gained a lot of experience.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:01.774
And overall, it
was very exciting,

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:02.942
and I'm happy with it.

00:04:03.008 --> 00:04:05.011
I'd say that's a matching set.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:09.047
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:11.350
Can you dig it?

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:12.684
Well, I certainly can.

00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:15.488
Your Spetsnaz shovels
look ready to go.

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:17.423
But what kind of lethal
damage can they do?

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.690
To find that out,
I'm going to take

00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:20.292
your shovels to deliver
some lethal blows

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:21.427
of this ballistics dummy.

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:22.328
Cameron, you're up first.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:23.162
You ready for this?

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.062
 Oh, yeah.

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:24.796
 All right.

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.665
Let's do this.

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:30.403
[music playing]

00:04:44.516 --> 00:04:46.919
All right, Cameron, let's talk
about your Spetsnaz shovels

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.254
here.

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:50.422
The weight is right, but
there is a little bit

00:04:50.522 --> 00:04:52.759
of issue with your handles.

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:53.926
They're too smooth.

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.194
A couple of times,
it really felt

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:56.796
like it wanted to slip out.

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.330
They delivered nice cuts.

00:04:58.397 --> 00:05:00.599
Thrusts are very effective.

00:05:00.699 --> 00:05:03.602
And overall sir, it will kill.

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:05.104
 Yes.

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:06.205
 All right, Mike,
your turn, sir.

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:06.972
You ready?

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:08.941
 I'm ready.

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:12.578
[music playing]

00:05:28.026 --> 00:05:29.295
 All right, Mike.

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:30.863
Let's talk about your
Spetsnaz shovels here.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.432
These are razor sharp.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:35.601
Your handle construction-- the
one thing I didn't care for

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:36.802
was it's round.

00:05:36.902 --> 00:05:38.737
When it's round, it can
go in different ways,

00:05:38.804 --> 00:05:40.372
and I have to constantly
make adjustments.

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:42.241
But because of the ribbing
that you have there,

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:44.277
I was able to hold
on to it quite well.

00:05:44.343 --> 00:05:48.047
Overall sir, your
shovels will kill.

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.516
 Awesome.

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:52.218
 All right, gentlemen,
you know what time it is.

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:53.419
It's time for the
strength test--

00:05:53.485 --> 00:05:55.788
what we're calling
our throwing chop.

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:57.590
What I'm going to
be doing is throwing

00:05:57.657 --> 00:06:00.125
your shovels into our targets
and then chopping on our fence

00:06:00.192 --> 00:06:01.460
here.

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:02.995
What this is about is
not what your shovels do

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:05.531
to these targets, but what these
targets can do to your shovels.

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:06.432
Cameron, you're up first.

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:07.199
Are you ready?

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:07.899
 Yeah.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.035
Let's do this.

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:13.773
[music playing]

00:06:26.118 --> 00:06:27.286
 All right, Cameron.

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:28.554
For throwing, the
smooth handle is great.

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:30.256
That's not a plus
for chopping though.

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:32.324
When I'm chopping,
I'm constantly

00:06:32.424 --> 00:06:34.193
kind of pulling it
back into my hand

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.162
because it wants
to slide forward.

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:41.433
This right here, this thin spot
where you've got that hammer,

00:06:41.533 --> 00:06:43.202
it took a roll right there.

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:44.637
They threw well.

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:45.337
Good job.

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:46.538
 Thank you very much.

00:06:46.605 --> 00:06:47.639
 All right, Mike.
You're up.

00:06:47.706 --> 00:06:48.774
You ready?
- Yeah, I'm ready.

00:06:48.874 --> 00:06:50.776
 OK.

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:54.414
[music playing]

00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:13.232
OK.

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:14.834
So right off the bat, the
finish work is really nice.

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:17.036
Your sockets are
really beautiful.

00:07:17.102 --> 00:07:18.070
They threw great.

00:07:18.137 --> 00:07:19.672
They certainly chopped fine.

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:22.774
I don't see any issues with
the edge of your blade at all.

00:07:22.841 --> 00:07:24.677
These are definitely
well-made tools.

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:25.243
Good job.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:26.112
 Thank you.

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:29.615
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:07:29.681 --> 00:07:33.485
This is a sharpness
test, the sandman slice.

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:35.354
Now unlike the strength
test, this is all about what

00:07:35.454 --> 00:07:38.090
your weapons do to the sandman.

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:38.991
Cameron, you're up first.

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:39.725
You ready for this?

00:07:39.826 --> 00:07:40.258
 Let's do this.

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:42.495
 Let's do this.

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:46.132
[music playing]

00:08:03.616 --> 00:08:04.950
All right, Cameron.

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:07.353
No issues with slashing and
chopping on the sandman.

00:08:07.453 --> 00:08:10.256
Sir, your weapons will cut.

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:11.457
All right, Mike.
Your turn, sir.

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:12.191
You ready?

00:08:12.291 --> 00:08:13.892
 I'm ready.

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:17.563
[music playing]

00:08:30.575 --> 00:08:31.644
 All right, Mike.

00:08:31.744 --> 00:08:33.579
Your edges are sharp.

00:08:33.645 --> 00:08:36.148
Every cut was deep
and sliced nicely.

00:08:36.215 --> 00:08:38.049
Overall sir, it will cut.

00:08:38.116 --> 00:08:38.918
 Thank you.

00:08:42.554 --> 00:08:43.990
 Well, gentlemen, you
guys should both be

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:45.224
very proud of yourselves.

00:08:45.291 --> 00:08:47.559
We put your Spetsnaz shovels
through very hard tests.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:48.694
As you know, there
can only be one

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:50.763
champion of "Forged in Fire."

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:57.469
Today's champion is Mike.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:58.738
Congratulations.

00:08:58.838 --> 00:09:00.306
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:00.406 --> 00:09:02.408
Cameron, unfortunately, that
means you didn't win today,

00:09:02.475 --> 00:09:03.876
and Dave is going
to tell you why.

00:09:03.942 --> 00:09:05.911
 Cameron, what this came
down to is really two things--

00:09:06.011 --> 00:09:08.714
your handle being as slippery
as it was and the damage

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:09.981
you took in the strength test.

00:09:10.048 --> 00:09:11.817
For those reasons,
we're letting you go.

00:09:11.884 --> 00:09:12.784
 All right.

00:09:12.851 --> 00:09:13.853
 Cameron, you
definitely have what

00:09:13.919 --> 00:09:15.187
it takes to fight in the forge.

00:09:15.288 --> 00:09:16.989
You made it from
four down to two.

00:09:17.089 --> 00:09:17.923
It was a close call.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.425
But your time in
the forge has ended.

00:09:19.492 --> 00:09:20.659
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:22.093
step off the forge floor.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:23.329
 Thank you.

00:09:23.396 --> 00:09:24.830
 Take care, Cam.

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:26.932
 I wanted to win it really
badly to prove to myself that I

00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:28.667
can really go up
to the standards

00:09:28.767 --> 00:09:31.903
as what other ABS master
smiths are able to do.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:34.039
This experience,
it's really amazing,

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:36.541
and I couldn't have
asked for more.

00:09:36.608 --> 00:09:37.977
 Mike, congratulations.

00:09:38.043 --> 00:09:40.513
That means you are today's
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:40.613 --> 00:09:43.381
You'll be getting a
check for $10,000.

00:09:43.482 --> 00:09:44.482
Congratulations.

00:09:44.549 --> 00:09:46.085
 Thank you.

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:49.355
I'm feeling amazing, like,
on top of the world amazing.

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:52.091
 Mike, I was really impressed
on the finish you got on those.

00:09:52.157 --> 00:09:53.892
It's really nice, clean
from top to bottom.

00:09:53.959 --> 00:09:54.426
Well done.

00:09:54.526 --> 00:09:55.461
 Thank you.

00:09:55.561 --> 00:09:56.595
I build knives for a hobby.

00:09:56.662 --> 00:09:57.963
From this point on
though, I really

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:01.366
want to concentrate on
doing real high end work

00:10:01.433 --> 00:10:03.502
and just improve my skills.

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:07.006
[music playing]

